  "findings": [
    "Adjective counts show weak differences; adjacent-adjective and positive-lexicon differences are especially small. Superlatives are lower, not higher, on average in AI passages.",
    "First-person words are less frequent on average in AI passages. A pronoun count is not a measurement of personalization.",
    "Newline rate, sentence-size statistics and a tail of extreme word repetition warrant controlled modeling; source and domain shifts can invalidate these signals.",
    "POS predictability is testable with training-only cross-fitted class models, but a mode mismatch is not an actual grammatical mistake. No semantic claims about poetry, authenticity or factual accuracy are tested."
